<description>
Slide every colored domino straight toward the full red edge wall until it is blocked.

Input structure
- The background is empty space.
- One non-background color forms a complete one-cell-thick edge wall and appears nowhere else.
- Every other foreground object is a monochromatic 4-connected domino, either horizontal or vertical.

Rule
- Keep the edge wall fixed and clear the other foreground objects from their original positions.
- The wall side gives the gravity direction: objects move up, down, left, or right toward that wall.
- Settle dominoes nearest the wall first; each domino slides rigidly along the gravity direction until the next step would hit the wall, another settled domino, or the grid boundary.

Key insight
- The full edge wall is the only anchor; the output is the gravity-packed state of all remaining dominoes against that wall.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "each non-wall monochrome domino object s",
  "path": "straight toward the complete red edge wall, perpendicular to that edge, stopping when the next step would hit the wall, a settled domino, or the grid boundary",
  "trajectory": "move s rigidly to its stopped endpoint, preserving shape and color",
  "transform": "clear s.old cells to background; keep the red edge wall unchanged",
  "multi_step": "settle dominoes nearest the wall first so farther dominoes stack behind them"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 5-10 rows x 5-11 cols
  background: 0 (black)
  wall:
    description: one complete edge (top/bottom/left/right) filled with a single non-bg color
    color: 2 [observed]; any non-bg color that appears nowhere else in the grid
    sides: all four sides observed across examples
  dominoes:
    count: 5-11 per grid
    shape: exactly 2 cells, 4-connected (horizontal or vertical)
    colors: non-bg, non-wall; multiple dominoes may share a color
    placement: no two dominoes touch (min Manhattan gap >= 2); no domino overlaps the wall row/col
    mix: both horizontal and vertical orientations present
  output:
    wall: unchanged
    dominoes: slid rigidly toward the wall until blocked by wall, another settled domino, or grid boundary
    settle_order: nearest-to-wall first; farther dominoes stack behind closer ones
    original positions: cleared to background

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first, then scatter
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size (5-10 x 5-11) and a random wall side (top/bottom/left/right).
    2. Fill the wall edge with a chosen wall color.
    3. Build the settled (output) state by packing 5-11 dominoes against the wall.
       Place dominoes one at a time adjacent to the wall or to already-placed dominoes,
       ensuring no overlap. Mix horizontal and vertical orientations.
    4. Record each domino's settled position as the output.
    5. For each domino, compute a random slide-back distance (1 to max available space
       away from wall along the gravity axis) to get its input position. Ensure no
       input-position overlaps or adjacencies between dominoes (min gap >= 2 cells).
    6. Build the input grid: wall + dominoes at scattered positions, rest background.
```
</generation_spec>
